Rewritten: the measurement and the fix. The account-scoped catalog read
(chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/models, asked with the sign-in's own headers),
the per-model table of advertised window against published ceiling against
what a probe accepted, the bisection probe that reads a late SSE error frame
for context_length_exceeded, the 900,000 default and the 918,000 clamp, and
the 2026-10-14 measurement of gpt-6.1-sol (919,956 accepted, 930,151
refused) are the original's, kept as numbers with the date on them. The write
moved from Hermes' model_overrides to the lever Nodecode documents,
providers.<id>.models[].context_window, through the shared config's own atomic
writer, and revert takes back exactly the values apply wrote and no others.
The sign-in is read the way the original read it through its host: the cell
never handles a refresh, only the access token the store already holds, and
an environment variable can stand in for it. The Python is Common Lisp here:
nlk:http in place of the Hermes credentialed-request helper, one section
declaration in place of the plugin's config schema, nlk:define-contract for
the tool's arguments, and one manual topic in place of the bundled skill.

Left out: image generation through the subscription. The original drove
core's own Codex-backed image provider - it selected it and proved the route,
never reimplemented the request - and Nodecode has its own image_gen choice
and image cells, so selecting a provider from here would fight them. Also left
out: the CLI subcommand tree (hermes codex-truly status/models/apply/revert/
probe/image) and its argparse surface, which the /codex-truly command and the
tool carry here; the bundled SKILL.md, which is the manual topic; the
`apply_to_base_slugs` opt-in and the `-900k` picker variants, which are
Hermes' own naming of a widened model and have no counterpart in Nodecode's
config; and the pytest suite, replaced by this folder's offline test system.
